[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/irungentoo/Xiaomi_Yi_4k_Camera/issues/comments/307211325","html_url":"https://github.com/irungentoo/Xiaomi_Yi_4k_Camera/issues/17#issuecomment-307211325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/irungentoo/Xiaomi_Yi_4k_Camera/issues/17","id":307211325,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzIxMTMyNQ==","user":{"login":"somacoder","id":25708712,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NzA4NzEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25708712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder","html_url":"https://github.com/somacoder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/somacoder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-06-08T20:01:18Z","updated_at":"2017-06-08T20:01:18Z","body":"The problem appears to be that all Yi 4k cameras show up as having the same \"Device Instance Path\". Since they are not unique, when the second one is plugged in, Windows fails to recognize it as a new device. More specifically, this may be related to the \"serial number\" suffix at the end of the instance path. The assignment of this should be uniquely fed from the device, but again, all Yi 4K devices appear to have the same one to Windows. Not sure if this could help anyone to garner a solution. I hope so. I've got nothing so far.\r\n\r\nHere is the Instance Path for all Yi 4K cameras in Windows: \r\nUSBSTOR\\DISK&VE